WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
In 1373, an English
woman, Julian of Norwich,

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.170
had a series of visions.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.210
She wrote them up as a book.

4
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.450
Far away, Sufi Muslims spoke of
the self passing away in God.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.550
Paul writes that he was caught
up into the third heaven,

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.040
and heard unspeakable words.

7
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.240
In 1902, William James
gathered reports like these.

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.300
Mystics kept saying their
experience defies expression.

9
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.860
So if it cannot be put into words, how
do mystics fill whole books describing

10
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:32.720
it?

11
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.970
In this mission, you'll test James'
four marks of a mystical experience.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.520
Then you'll weigh three
readings of one report:

13
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.090
union, illusion, or the body at work.

14
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.480
Your mission: explain how mystics can
describe what they say cannot be described.
